From 4b1ff364609f089714e20db8e2e6c031f1c21a60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 08:47:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Scorecard: give each fresh analysis module its own include
 and eval (fixes 077 under Julia 1.13)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Julia 1.13's Module(name) defines neither include nor eval, so every analysis script failed at its first
include("../config.jl") with "UndefVarError: `include` not defined in Main.scorecard_…". Both are now defined in the
module before the script is included; include stays relative to the including file.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Abhhvmoet3Py5umLctXSCh
---
 analysis/scorecard_functions.jl | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/analysis/scorecard_functions.jl b/analysis/scorecard_functions.jl
index e4a0028..7bf02dd 100644
--- a/analysis/scorecard_functions.jl
+++ b/analysis/scorecard_functions.jl
@@ -37,6 +37,11 @@ function run_in_fresh_module(script, args)
     append!(ARGS, args)
     try
         sandbox = Module(Symbol("scorecard_", splitext(basename(script))[1]))
+        # Julia 1.13's Module() has no include or eval of its own (unlike a `module … end` block): give it both, so the
+        # scripts' include("../config.jl") works (relative to the including file, as usual)
+        Core.eval(sandbox, :(eval(x) = Core.eval($sandbox, x)))
+        Core.eval(sandbox, :(include(path::AbstractString) = Base.include($sandbox, path)))
+        Core.eval(sandbox, :(include(mapexpr::Function, path::AbstractString) = Base.include(mapexpr, $sandbox, path)))
         Base.include(sandbox, script)
     finally
         empty!(ARGS)
